# Runtime artifacts a run materializes locally — never part of the config.
# The config layer is TRACKED on purpose (issue #29): config.ts holds project
# decisions (labelBases, chainableBases, queue labels, base branch) that belong
# in review and in history — diffable, restorable, visible to every clone and
# to agents working in linked worktrees. Only what a machine generates below
# stays out: secrets (.env*), logs, agent worktrees, the out-of-tree Engine
# install (#22) and its standalone lockfiles (#23). The examples are negated
# back in so `git archive` keeps shipping the templates.
.env*
!.env*.example
logs/
worktrees/
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
